-- title:
--   Local Hecke set at a split prime has q+1 classes
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ that are maximal among orders with respect to inclusion, the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ being $N$. Let $q$ and $q'$ be primes with $q'\neq q$ and $q\nmid N$, and assume $a<0$, $b<0$ and that for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime containing $q$, write $H_v=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ and let $B_v=$ [`Submodule.localBox R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) be the additive subgroup of $H_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$. Then the set of classes in $H_v^{\times}$ modulo the stabiliser of $B_v$ (for the multiplication action of $H_v^{\times}$ on subsets of $H_v$) that are represented by some unit $g$ with $g\in B_v$, $q\cdot g^{-1}\in B_v$, $g^{-1}\notin B_v$ and $q^{-1}\cdot g\notin B_v$ is finite of cardinality exactly $q+1$.
--
--   This is the local degree of the Hecke operator $T_q$ for an Eichler order in a definite quaternion algebra: the elements of the local order with elementary divisors $(1,q)$ fall into $q+1$ classes modulo the local unit group, matching the $q+1$ points of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$. It feeds the identification of the prime Hecke set with a double coset of the local stabiliser and the corresponding counting statement on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsEichlerOrder_natCard_setOf_exists_quotientMk_stabilizer_localBox_eq_eq_succ.lean

